---
title: "AWS EventBridge"
description: "Send events to an Amazon EventBridge event bus, matched by rules you configure in AWS."
---

Send events to an Amazon EventBridge event bus.

## Creating an EventBridge Destination

```sh
curl '{% $OUTPOST_API_BASE_URL %}/tenants/<TENANT_ID>/destinations' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>' \
--data '{
  "type": "aws_eventbridge",
  "topics": ["orders"],
  "config": {
    "event_bus_name": "my-bus",
    "region": "us-east-1"
  },
  "credentials": {
    "key": "<AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID>",
    "secret": "<AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY>"
  }
}'
```

## Configuration

### Config

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `config.event_bus_name` | string | No | The event bus name or ARN. Leave empty to use the account's default event bus. |
| `config.region` | string | Yes | AWS region (e.g., `us-east-1`) |
| `config.endpoint` | string | No | Custom endpoint URL (for LocalStack, etc.) |

### Credentials

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `credentials.key` | string | No | AWS Access Key ID |
| `credentials.secret` | string | No | AWS Secret Access Key |
| `credentials.session` | string | No | AWS Session Token (for temporary credentials) |

Credentials are optional on the destination itself so that a future credential-less publishing mode (the kind some AWS-partnered SaaS platforms use) can be added later without a breaking config change. Today, publishing always requires a working AWS Access Key/Secret pair — leaving them empty results in every publish attempt failing with an authorization error, not a silent fallback to some other credential source.

## Event Format

Each Outpost event is published as a single EventBridge entry:

- **Source** is fixed for the whole deployment, not configured per destination.
- **DetailType** is the event's topic.
- **Detail** is a JSON object containing `metadata` and the event's `data` field:

```json
{
  "metadata": {
    "event-id": "evt_123",
    "topic": "orders",
    "timestamp": "1704067200"
  },
  "data": {
    "order_id": "123",
    "status": "created"
  }
}
```

{% tabs tabGroup="deployment" %}
{% tab label="Managed" %}
Configure `DESTINATIONS_EVENTBRIDGE_SOURCE` in the Config API or in [Hookdeck Outpost Destinations settings](https://dashboard.hookdeck.com/settings/project/destinations) to change the `Source` value stamped on every published event. Defaults to `outpost`.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Self-Hosted" %}
Set `DESTINATIONS_EVENTBRIDGE_SOURCE` to change the `Source` value stamped on every published event. Defaults to `outpost`.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

## IAM Permissions

The IAM user or role requires:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": "events:PutEvents",
    "Resource": "arn:aws:events:*:*:event-bus/my-bus"
  }]
}
```
